  {
    "id": 2,
    "slug": "choosing-a-dotnet-client-ui-framework",
    "title": "Choosing a .NET Client UI Framework",
    "topic": "UI Frameworks",
    "summary": "A decision guide for where to write a .NET client app today, with support dates and state read from the primary sources (the Windows developer FAQ, the MAUI support policy, the WPF and WinForms what's new pages): WinUI 3, .NET MAUI, WPF, WinForms, Blazor Hybrid and Blazor in the browser, plus Avalonia and Uno in a short table. Measured on macOS arm64 with SDK 10.0.100 and 11.0.100: which client templates exist, what the MAUI workload requires, WPF and WinForms projects that compile but cannot run off Windows, a WPF app hosting Blazor and a Blazor WebAssembly publish, with the rest marked docs only.",
